joa_1_1_1_popup4_gp.message:
[I=hud_element_water,1] #element_water;
On its own, this element usually forms sprays or waves of water. It doesn't inflict any damage, but it can make things wet, put out fires, and push things around.

Conjure #element_water; by pressing [K=water]. Then, when you're ready to soak something, simply aim with [K=spell_forward] to spray in the direction of your choice.

joa_1_1_2_popup8kb.message:
[I=hud_element_cold,1] #element_cold;
This element both chills and injures most denizens of Midgård, and can also be used to turn #element_water; into #element_ice;. Skate across rivers and lakes, or freeze some wet fellow in his tracks. You can even freeze the #element_water; in your spell queue...

Conjure some #element_cold; by pressing [K=cold] a few times. With this spell in your spell queue, you can freeze #element_water; by [c]area-casting[/c] [K=spell_aoe] or [c]forward-casting[/c] [K=spell_forward] the spell. Its very convenience may well be the reason that wizards can't swim!

